**Suggestions (10, -$247/mo)**

- suggest `DbMultiAZ`: -$132/mo, Single-AZ instance and storage, for development stacks: no standby, so an AZ failure or maintenance takes the database down (now db.m6g.large postgres Multi-AZ)
- suggest `DbMultiAZ`: -$1.40/mo, gp3 (now storage)
- suggest `Big`: -$22/mo, gp3 with 6000 IOPS and 250 MiB/s, gp2's baseline (now EBS gp2 storage)
- suggest `Db`: -$13/mo, db.m6g.large (Graviton) (now db.m5.large postgres Single-AZ)
- suggest `Server`: -$15/mo, m6g.large (Graviton), if the AMI and software run on arm64 (now m5.large on-demand (Linux))
- suggest `Server`: -$2.10/mo, gp3 (now EBS gp2 storage)
- suggest `Service`: -$15/mo, ARM64 vCPU and memory (Graviton, RuntimePlatform CpuArchitecture), if the image is built for arm64 (now Fargate vCPU (2 tasks))
- suggest `NatB`: -$37/mo, one NAT Gateway for the VPC instead of 2 (CDK natGateways: 1); egress then depends on one AZ (now NAT Gateway)
- suggest `Cache`: -$1.46/mo, cache.t4g.micro (Graviton) (now cache.t3.micro Redis)
- suggest `Endpoint`: -$8.03/mo, one subnet instead of 2, for development stacks: clients in the other AZs then cross AZs and lose the endpoint if its AZ fails (now interface endpoint)

